## Summary
The Italian Supervisory Authority fined Eni Gas e Luce a total of €11.5 million for multiple violations of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). The fines, announced on January 17, 2020, were imposed by the Italian Supervisory Authority (ISA) and reported in a post on GDPR.eu.

## Key Points
- Eni Gas e Luce received two fines totaling €11.5 million, with amounts of €8.5 million and €3 million.
- The fines were imposed for violations related to GDPR regulations.
- The Italian Supervisory Authority (ISA) is the entity responsible for imposing the fines.
- The announcement of the fines occurred on January 17, 2020.


